## honeybadger-io/honeybadger-elixir/issues/475
:breadcrumbs_enabled blowing up logs, consider putting elsewhere 2023-03-14 closed
Our logs go to datadog and we use logging metadata to send extra context. Since turning on breadcrumbs its breaking logs when the data in hb_breadcrumbs is large enough to split the json line across multiple lines.

There doesnt seem to be a way to use breadcrumbs but move their storage out of the logger context. For now we have disabled breadcrumbs even though they add a ton of value.
## honeybadger-io/honeybadger-elixir/issues/487
Stop using logger metadata for breadcrumbs 2023-04-16 closed
Breadcrumbs used the logger metadata for convenient access to the process dictionary. That's not necessary, and it makes standard metadata logging unusable when shipping logs to a third party service.

This moves breadcrumb storage to a separate key in the process dictionary.

Closes #475
